<section>
    <h3>Redacting without damaging the response</h3>
    <pre style="font-size: 0.45em;"><code class="language-json" data-trim>
{"meta":{},"password":"x","n":1.0,"big":12345678901234567890}
    </code></pre>
    <div class="fragment">
        <p class="label-before">json_decode + json_encode</p>
        <pre style="font-size: 0.45em;"><code class="language-json" data-trim>
{"meta":[],"password":"[REDACTED]","n":1,"big":1.2345678901234567e+19}
        </code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment">
        <p class="label-after">In-place replacement</p>
        <pre style="font-size: 0.45em;"><code class="language-json" data-trim>
{"meta":{},"password":"[REDACTED]","n":1.0,"big":12345678901234567890}
        </code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="fragment callout">
        The JSON is no longer decoded then re-encoded: sensitive values are replaced in a single pass,
        the rest is <b>byte-for-byte identical</b> (<code>{}</code>, floats, big integers, escapes, formatting).
    </p>
    <aside class="notes">
        If the JSON were decoded then re-encoded, an assertSame on the body would pass in record mode and fail in replay mode: very hard to diagnose.
    </aside>
</section>
